@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderThickness 1
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam sequenceGroupFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceGroupFontStyle bold
skinparam noteFontSize 12
skinparam noteBorderColor #aaaaaa
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #fffef0
skinparam participantFontSize 13
skinparam participantBorderColor #41516a
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #EBF1FB
skinparam arrowColor #33445c
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Agentic IAM — Request Flow

participant "User / Codex" as U
participant "codex-jira-mcp-adapter\n(SPIFFE workload)" as A
participant "SPIRE" as SP
participant "capability-issuer-envoy" as CE
participant "capability-issuer\n(capiss)" as C
participant "OPA" as O
participant "jira-mcp-envoy" as ME
participant "jira-mcp-gateway\n(PEP)" as G
participant "Jira\n(mock / live)" as J

== Identity bootstrap (startup, repeated on rotation) ==

SP -> A : X.509 SVID\nspiffe://.../codex-jira-mcp-adapter\n(short-lived, auto-rotated)
SP -> G : X.509 SVID\nspiffe://.../jira-mcp-gateway

note over SP, A
  Every workload in the stack receives a SPIFFE identity from SPIRE.
  SVIDs are short-lived and rotated automatically.
  A workload that is not explicitly registered cannot obtain one.
end note

== Per-request: authority minting ==

U -> A : "summarise the IAM project"
note over A
  Translates instruction to precise intent:
  aud = jira-mcp-gateway
  act = read_project_summary
  res = jira-mcp:/project:IAM
end note

A -> CE : mTLS (SVID as client cert)\nmint request {aud, act, res}
CE -> C : verified caller SPIFFE ID\n+ mint request
C -> O : may spiffe://.../codex-jira-mcp-adapter\nmint {aud, act, res}?
O --> C : permit

C --> CE : Biscuit token\n{aud, act, res, sub, exp}
CE --> A : token

note over A
  Token stays inside the adapter.
  It is never returned to Codex,
  never logged, never sent upstream.
end note

== Per-request: authority enforcement ==

A -> ME : mTLS (SVID as client cert)\n+ capability token + call params
ME -> G : x-verified-spiffe-id: spiffe://.../codex-jira-mcp-adapter\n+ capability token + call params

note over G
  Enforces (all must pass — any failure → DENY, upstream never called):
  ① token signature valid and not expired
  ② token subject == x-verified-spiffe-id header
  ③ token audience == jira-mcp-gateway
  ④ token action == requested action
  ⑤ token resource == requested project key
  ⑥ call budget and rate allow this request
end note

G -> J : upstream API call\n(no capability token, no Codex credentials)
J --> G : response
G --> A : result
A --> U : MCP response\n(no tokens, no credentials, no raw Jira URLs)

@enduml
